  "difficulty_reason": "Beyond the universal inverse-Coxeter orbit giving the sharp lower bound, the type-D proof must control every signed-permutation orbit through a source-local monotone inverse-image process. Its essential new lemma handles passage through the central n/-n labels by excluding a half-circle of positions, and the complete final five-case argument identifies every possible terminal cycle configuration as a type-D noncrossing partition. This exceptional-centre dynamical termination construction is substantially beyond ordinary qualification-level permutation or antiexceedance counting.",
